## Problem

The v1 tag vocabulary hardcodes four values in Go source: needs-human,
deferred, post-talk, post-conference. The last two are personal calendar
labels that leaked into a reusable spec. No live ticket has ever used
them. More broadly, several settings are either hardcoded constants or
env-var-only with no project-level override.

## Design

A general INI-style config file `tickets/.ergrc`, created by `erg init`
with sensible defaults.

```ini
# Project configuration for git-erg.
# Created by: erg init

[tags]
# Tag vocabulary — one per line. All tags suppress `erg ready` output.
# Remove or add lines to fit your workflow.
needs-human
deferred

[update]
# url = https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MinhHaDuong/git-erg/main/tickets/erg
```

### Format

INI-style, minimal:
- `[section]` headers
- `key = value` pairs within sections (for scalar settings)
- Bare values within sections (for list settings like [tags])
- `#` line comments
- Blank lines ignored

No need for a third-party parser — this is ~40 lines of Go.

### Sections

| Section | Shape | What it replaces |
|---------|-------|------------------|
| `[tags]` | bare values (list) | validTagValues + skipReadyTags (compile-time maps) |
| `[update]` | key=value | ERG_UPDATE_URL env var / hardcoded updateURL constant |

Future sections (out of scope for this ticket):
- `[author]` — default author identity (currently ERG_AUTHOR / git config / $USER)

### Lookup and precedence

1. Env vars override config file (ERG_UPDATE_URL beats [update] url)
2. Config file: `$ERG_TICKET_DIR/.ergrc` (or discovered ticket dir)
3. Built-in defaults if config absent or section missing

### Validator behavior

- [tags] present → its values are the closed set
- [tags] absent → fall back to built-in: needs-human, deferred
- [tags] empty (section exists, no values) → no tags valid
- Unknown tag values still fail validation (closed-set contract preserved)

### erg ready behavior

All tags in the vocabulary suppress readiness. The two maps collapse
into one: the vocabulary IS the skip set.

## Actions

1. Add `loadConfig(dir string) -> Config` with section parsing
2. Add `.ergrc` to initAssetPaths and bootstrap_assets.go
3. Wire [tags] into validator (replaces validTagValues)
4. Wire [tags] into ready.go (replaces skipReadyTags)
5. Wire [update] url into cmdUpdate (replaces hardcoded updateURL)
6. Remove post-talk and post-conference from built-in defaults
7. Update spec-erg-v1.md and AGENTS.md
8. Update test fixtures

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg init` creates tickets/.ergrc with default [tags] and [update]
- [ ] Validator reads [tags] when present, falls back to defaults
- [ ] `erg ready` uses same vocabulary (one source of truth)
- [ ] `erg update` reads [update] url, env var still overrides
- [ ] post-talk and post-conference removed from defaults
- [ ] Tests cover: custom .ergrc, missing .ergrc fallback, empty [tags],
      env var overrides config
- [ ] `make check` passes
